</p><p>There were small upward effects to the change in the rate from 3 of the 11 food and non-alcoholic beverages classes, namely vegetables; milk, cheese and eggs (particularly cheese); and fish. These were partially offset by small downward effects from bread and cereals; and oils and fats.</p>
